{"id": "f5a5d115e0ed756f", "path": "lesson-plans/General/LESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES (2).docx", "title": "LESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES", "area": "lesson-plans", "level": "General", "format": "docx", "pages": null, "words": 5370, "text": "ner Download Christian values a href https drive google com uc export\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: CHRISTIAN VALUES\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: Honesty (Ananias and Sapphira)\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to narrate the story of Ananias and Sapphira and desire to be honest in\ntheir lives.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nHow do we celebrate Easter? Which activities take place during Easter?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Imagination and\ncreativity\n Learning to learn\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Honesty\n Trust\n Responsibility\n Sharing\nDecision making\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nGood news bible.\nProps and costumes for the role play.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 66-68.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Direct learners to the picture on page 66 of the learner’s book.\nStep 2: Direct learners to activity 1 and lead them through the questions.\nStep 3: Select some learners and help them to find and read the story from the bible.\nStep 4: Ask learners why it is good to tell the truth always and guide learners into appreciation that telling the truth\nis good.\nStep 5: Direct the learners through activity 2\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read summary notes.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer question and inform them of the next lesson.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nEncourage learners to practice honesty at home.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: CHRISTIAN VALUES\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: Honesty (Ananias and Sapphira)\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to narrate the story of Ananias and Sapphira and desire to be honest in\ntheir lives.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nHow do we celebrate Easter? Which activities take place during Easter?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Imagination and\ncreativity\n Learning to learn\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Honesty\n Trust\n Responsibility\n Sharing\nDecision making\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nGood news bible.\nProps and costumes for the role play.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 66-68.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Guide learners in pairs or groups to role play .\nStep 2: Select some learners and help them to find and read the story from the bible.\nStep 3: Using questions guide learners to internalize the lesson of the story.\nStep 4: Ask learners how they will always ensure that they are honest and direct learners to part 2 of activity 2.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read summary notes.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer question and inform them of the next lesson.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nEncourage learners to practice honesty at home.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: CHRISTIAN VALUES\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: Giving offering in church\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to practice honesty by taking offerings to church.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy should you be honest with church offering?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Self-efficacy\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Honesty\n Trust\n Responsibility\n Sharing\nDecision making\nSelf-esteem\nassertiveness\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nGood news bible.\nFlash cars with short descriptions of situations where the learners have to choose between being honest or disobedient or\ndishonest with their church offerings.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 68-69.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Remind the learners of the illustration of Jane giving offering in church on page 66 and ask learners to\nactivity 3 .\nStep 2: Select some learners and help them to find and read the story from the bible.\nStep 3: Guide learners to the understanding that the story of Ananias and Sapphira teaches us to be honest in giving\nofferings in church.\nStep 4: Lead the learners to commit to being honest with their offerings in church and learners to copy the notes in\ntheir books.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read summary notes.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer question and inform them of the next lesson.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nEncourage learners to practice honesty at home.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: CHRISTIAN VALUES\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: Giving offering in church\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to practice honesty by taking offerings to church.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy should you be honest with church offering?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Self-efficacy\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Honesty\n Trust\n Responsibility\n Sharing\nDecision making\nSelf-esteem\nassertiveness\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nGood news bible.\nFlash cars with short descriptions of situations where the learners have to choose between being honest or disobedient or\ndishonest with their church offerings.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 68-69.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Remind the learners of the illustration of Jane giving offering in church on page 66 and ask learners to\nactivity 3\nStep 2: Select some learners and help them to find and read the story from the bible.\nStep 3: Guide learners to the understanding that the story of Ananias and Sapphira teaches us to be honest in giving\nofferings in church.\nStep 4: Lead the learners to commit to being honest with their offerings in church and learners to copy the notes in\ntheir books.\nStep 5: Guide learners to do activity 4\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read summary notes.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer question and inform them of the next lesson.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nEncourage learners to practice honesty at home.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: CHRISTIAN VALUES\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: Respecting other people’s items\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to explain the importance of respecting other people’s items for\nharmonious living.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhat do you do when you find lost items?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Self-efficacy\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Imagination and\ncreativity\n Honesty\n Respect\n Responsibility\nDecision making\nSelf-esteem\nassertiveness\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nGood news bible.\nFlash cars with situations requiring respect for other people’s items.\nLearner’s tablets.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 70-71.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Direct the attention of the learners to the key inquiry question and ask them to carry out activity 5.\nStep 2: Using questions, remind learners of the story Ananias and Sapphira\nStep 3: Guide learners to know that taking and keeping a lost item is cheating.\nStep 4: Guide learners to commit to not keeping for themselves lost items that they may come across and direct them\nto activity 6.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read summary notes.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer question and inform them of the next lesson.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nEncourage learners to practice honesty at home.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: CHRISTIAN VALUES\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: Respecting other people’s items\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to explain the importance of respecting other people’s items for\nharmonious living.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhat do you do when you find lost items?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Self-efficacy\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Imagination and\ncreativity\n Honesty\n Respect\n Responsibility\nDecision making\nSelf-esteem\nassertiveness\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nGood news bible.\nFlash cars with situations requiring respect for other people’s items.\nLearner’s tablets.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 70-71.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Ask learners how they feel if someone took their items or used them without first asking for permission.\nStep 2: Using questions, remind learners of what happened to Ananias and Sapphira after they died.\nStep 3: Lead learners to appreciate that when they take other people’s items or use them without permission they are\nnot honest or respectful.\nStep 4: Guide learners to commit to never taking or using other people’s items without their permission.\nStep 5: Present some situations to the learners and ask them to state what would be the honest thing to do in those\nsituations.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read summary notes.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer question and inform them of the next lesson.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nEncourage learners to practice honesty at home.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: CHRISTIAN VALUES\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: Thankfulness\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to describe ways if thanking God for creating them.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nHow can I thank God for creating me?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Self-efficacy\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Imagination and\ncreativity\n Learning to learn\n Thankfulness\n Humility\n Trust\n Responsibility\nDecision making\nSelf-esteem\nSelf-awareness\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nGood news bible.\nChart showing ways in which to thank God for creating us.\nManila paper, crayons.\nLearner’s tablets.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 72-73.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Call the attention of the learners the Key inquiry questions and direct them to undertake Activity 1.\nStep 2: Select some learners to read out loud the Bible verse.\nStep 3: Lead learners to appreciate that the bible tells them to thank God for His love\nStep 4: Guide learners to appreciate the love that God has shown them by creating them and therefore commit to\nthanking Him.\nStep 5: Put up the chart and work with the learners to identify ways in which they can thank God for creating them.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read summary notes.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer question and inform them of the next lesson.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nEncourage learners to make “thank you” cards.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: CHRISTIAN VALUES\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: Thankfulness\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to describe ways if thanking God for creating them.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nHow can I thank God for creating me?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Self-efficacy\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Imagination and\ncreativity\n Learning to learn\n Thankfulness\n Humility\n Trust\n Responsibility\nDecision making\nSelf-esteem\nSel-awareness\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nGood news bible.\nChart showing ways in which to thank God for creating us.\nManila paper, crayons.\nLearner’s tablets.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 72-73.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Direct learners to the Memory verse on page 73 of the learner’s book\nStep 2: Guide learners to mention the various ways they will thank God for creating them and appreciate that it is\ntheir responsibility to thank God for creating them.\nStep 3: Direct learners to activity 2.\nStep 4: Learners to share and discuss their work with the learners close to them.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read summary notes.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer question and inform them of the next lesson.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nEncourage learners to make “thank you” cards.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: CHRISTIAN VALUES\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: Thanking God for other people\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to thank God for their family, friends and teachers, and appreciate them\nall the time.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy should I thank God for other people?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Self-efficacy\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Imagination and\ncreativity\n Thankfulness\n Humility\n Trust\n Responsibility\nDecision making\nSelf-esteem\nSelf-awareness\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nGood news bible.\nFlash cards showing reasons for thanking God for other people.\nManila paper, crayons.\nLearner’s tablets.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 74-75.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Ask learners whether they thank God for their families, friends and teachers and direct them to activity 3.\nStep 2: Remind learners of Psalms 136:1.\nStep 3: Guide learners to understand that these other people in their lives are a show of God’s love for them.\nStep 4: Lead learners to identify the various ways in which they can thank God for the people in their lives and\ndirect them to activity 4.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read summary notes.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer question and inform them of the next lesson.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nEncourage learners to make “thank you” cards.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: CHRISTIAN VALUES\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: Forgiveness (the story of the unforgiving servant)\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to describe the story of the unforgiving servant and relate it to their\ninteraction with others.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhat did the unforgiving servant do? What do we learn from the story of the unforgiving servant?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Learning to learn\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Imagination and\ncreativity\n Citizenship\n Forgiveness\n Love\n Humility\n Tolerance\n Kindness, social justice\nDecision making\nSelf-esteem\nSelf-awareness\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nGood news bible.\nProps and costumes for role play.\nLearner’s tablets.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 74-75.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Direct learners attention to the key inquiry questions and to tackle part one of activity 1\nStep 2: Guide learners to undertake part two of activity 1.\nStep 3: Select some learners to read the story out aloud from the bible.\nStep 4: Guide the learners to see the wrong in how the unforgiving servant was forgiven but refused to forgive his\nfellow servant and lead learners to equate the story to God and themselves.\nStep 5: Direct learners to question 1 of Activity 2.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read summary notes.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer question and inform them of the next lesson.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nEncourage learners to observe within the school what happens when people do not forgive each other.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: CHRISTIAN VALUES\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: Forgiveness (the story of the unforgiving servant)\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to describe the story of the unforgiving servant and relate it to their\ninteraction with others.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhat did the unforgiving servant do? What do we learn from the story of the unforgiving servant?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Learning to learn\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Imagination and\ncreativity\n Citizenship\n Forgiveness\n Love\n Humility\n Tolerance\n Kindness, social justice\nDecision making\nSelf-esteem\nSelf-awareness\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nGood news bible.\nProps and costumes for role play\nLearner’s tablets.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 74-75.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Divide learners into groups and prepare them to role play.\nStep 2: Guide learners to understand that the unforgiving servant did wrong by refusing to forgive his fellow servant,\nand this is why he was punished by the King.\nStep 3: Ask learners whether they will forgive others and if so, how often.\nStep 4: Ask learners questions you prepared earlier about the story and the lessons from it.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read summary notes.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer question and inform them of the next lesson.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nEncourage learners to observe within the school what happens when people do not forgive each other.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: CHRISTIAN VALUES\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: Forgiving others\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to desire to forgive other in their day to day lives.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhat did the unforgiving servant do? What do we learn from the story of the unforgiving servant?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Learning to learn\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Self-efficacy\n Forgiveness\n Love\n Humility\n Tolerance\n Kindness, social justice\nDecision making\nSelf-esteem\nSelf-awareness\nassertiveness\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nGood news bible.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 78-79\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Direct learners to activity 3. Let them look at the pictures and read the story.\nStep 2: Select some learners to read Colossians 3:13 out loud.\nStep 3: Lead learners to understand that God wants us to forgive others in the same way he forgives us every time\nwe ask for His forgiveness.\nStep 4: Guide learners to control emotions in order to forgive and commit to forgiving others\nStep 5: Direct learners to the Memory verse on page 79 of the learner’s book.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read summary notes.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer question and inform them of the next lesson.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nEncourage learners to observe within the school what happens when people do not forgive each other.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: CHRISTIAN VALUES\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: Forgiving others\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to desire to forgive other in their day to day lives.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhat did the unforgiving servant do? What do we learn from the story of the unforgiving servant?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Learning to learn\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Self-efficacy\n Forgiveness\n Love\n Humility\n Tolerance\n Kindness, social justice\nDecision making\nSelf-esteem\nSelf-awareness\nassertiveness\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nGood news bible\nLearner’s Book 3 page 78-79\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Inform learners that they shall listen to someone tell them what happens when people don’t forgive each\nother.\nStep 2: Invite the speaker to begin. After he/she is done, encourage the learners to ask any questions before excusing\nhim/her.\nStep 3: Select some learners to recite Colossians 3:13.\nStep 4: Guide learners to understand that in order to be able to forgive others we must have humility, love for others\nand tolerance.\nStep 5: Direct learners to the I wonder question and lead them in imagining the scenario. Later direct them to\nactivity 4 and let them show what they would do in each situation\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read summary notes.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer question and inform them of the next lesson.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nEncourage learners to observe within the school what happens when people do not forgive each other.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: CHRISTIAN VALUES\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: Trust\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to:\n1. Identify people they can trust for their own safety.\n2. Mention the people to report to incase of danger for appropriate action to be taken.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWho are the people you trust?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Learning to learn\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Self-efficacy\n Critical thinking\n Trust\n Integrity\n Responsibility\nDecision making\nSelf-esteem\nSelf-awareness\nassertiveness\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nGood news bible.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 80-81.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Use questions to direct the learners to the meaning of the word “trust”. Draw the attention of the learners to\nthe key inquiry question.\nStep 2: Direct learners to activity 1. Let them look at the pictures then attempt to answer questions that follow.\nStep 3: Lead learners in identifying other people they can trust and report to when they are in danger.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read summary notes.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer question and inform them of the next lesson.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nEncourage learners to practice what to do in case they are in danger.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: CHRISTIAN VALUES\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: Trust\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to:\n1. Identify people they can trust for their own safety.\n2. Mention the people to report to incase of danger for appropriate action to be taken.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWho are the people you trust?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Learning to learn\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Self-efficacy\n Critical thinking\n Trust\n Integrity\n Responsibility\nDecision making\nSelf-esteem\nSelf-awareness\nassertiveness\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nGood news bible\nLearner’s Book 3 page 80-81\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Group learners accordingly.\nStep 2: Direct learners to activity 2. Let them read the scenarios and answer the questions.\nStep 3: Encourage learners to make their inputs after each dramatization, stating whether they agree with the actions\ntaken and why.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read summary notes.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer question and inform them of the next lesson.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nEncourage learners to practice what to do in case they are in danger.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: CHRISTIAN VALUES\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: Talking about others\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to discuss the effects of talking about others for harmonious living.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy is it wrong to talk about others?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Learning to learn\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Self-efficacy\n Critical thinking\n Trust\n Integrity\n Responsibility\n Love\n Respect\nDecision making\nEmpathy\nSelf-awareness\nFriendship formation\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nGood news bible.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 82-83.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Bring to the attention of the learners the key inquiry questions.\nStep 2: Direct learners to activity 3. Let them look at the picture and answer the questions.\nStep 3: inform the learners that the Bible guides us on talking about others.\nStep 4: Select some learners to take turns reading the verse from the Bible.\nStep 5: Guide the learners to talk about what they think the bible verse means. Lead learners to appreciate that\ngossiping causes hurt and conflict.\nStep 6: Ask them what they will do when someone wants them to gossip, and lead them state and demonstrate that\nthey will refuse. Direct learners to activity 4.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read summary notes.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer question and inform them of the next lesson.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nEncourage learners to practice what to do in case they are in danger.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: CHRISTIAN VALUES\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: Talking about others\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to discuss the effects of talking about others for harmonious living.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy is it wrong to talk about others?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Learning to learn\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Self-efficacy\n Critical thinking\n Trust\n Integrity\n Responsibility\n Love\n Respect\nDecision making\nEmpathy\nSelf-awareness\nFriendship formation\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nGood news bible.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 82-83\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION.\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Have learners stand up from their desks and sing and dance to the song.\nStep 2: Direct learners attention to the song under activity 5.\nStep 3: Have some learners read Proverbs 11:13.\nStep 4: Guide learners to appreciate that gossiping destroys trust; they cannot be trusted if they gossip.\nStep 5: Have the learners agree to always put themselves in the other person’s position before they gossip.\nStep 6: Pose the question you prepared earlier to the learners to gauge how well they have acquired knowledge on\nthe value of trust.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read summary notes.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer question and inform them of the next lesson.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nEncourage learners to practice what to do in case they are in danger.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: CHRISTIAN VALUES\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: Responsibility\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to discuss the importance of personal hygiene for healthy living.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy should I always keep myself clean and neat?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Self-efficacy\n Hard work\n Responsibility\n Concern\nDecision making\nEmpathy\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nGood news bible.\nManila paper.\nCrayons.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 84-85.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Ask learners what they did today in the morning before they left home.\nStep 2: Direct learners attention to the Key inquiry questions.\nStep 3: Direct learners to activity 1. Have them look at the pictures before they attempt answering the questions that\nfollow.\nStep 4: using their responses lead learners to understand that when they keep themselves and their immediate\nenvironment clean, they avoid germs that cause diseases.\nStep 5: Direct learners to the first question of Activity 2.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read summary notes.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer question and inform them of the next lesson.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nEncourage learners to look out for each other and correct each other while they are in school.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: CHRISTIAN VALUES\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: Responsibility\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to discuss the importance of personal hygiene for healthy living.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy should I always keep myself clean and neat?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Self-efficacy\n Hard work\n Responsibility\n Concern\nDecision making\nEmpathy\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nGood news bible.\nManila paper.\nCrayons.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 84-85.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Guide the learners to know that taking care of their cleanliness helps them avoid diseases and parasites such\nas lice, bed bugs and jiggers.\nStep 2: Lead learners to understand that personal cleanliness requires that they be responsible and do things without\nbeing told.\nStep 3: Direct learners to the second question of activity 2.Distibute the Manila paper and crayons and let the\nlearners create the posters.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read summary notes.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer question and inform them of the next lesson.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nEncourage learners to look out for each other and correct each other while they are in school.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: CHRISTIAN VALUES\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: Correcting others\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be able to acquire the value of responsibility by correcting those in the\nwrong.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhat should you do when you see someone doing wrong?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Citizenship\n Critical thinking and\nproblem solving\n Imagination and\ncreativity\n Trust , love\n Responsibility\n Concern\n Empathy\n Honesty\nDecision making\nEmpathy\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nAssertiveness\nProblem solving\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nGood news bible.\nCharts with the verse (Philippians 2:4) written on it.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 86-87.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Call the attention of the learners to the key inquiry questions on page 86 of learner’s book.\nStep 2: Direct learners to activity 3 and have them look at the pictures before answering the questions that follow.\nStep 3: Ask learners to say what they would do if they found their siblings or close friends doing wrong.\nStep 4: Select some learners to read the verse from the Bible.\nStep 5: Guide the learners to understand that when they care about someone, they do not let them do wrong.\nStep 6: Lead learners to understand that the first step in correcting someone is to ask them to stop doing wrong.\nDirect learners to the memory verse.\nStep 7: Direct learners to activity 4.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read summary notes.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer question and inform them of the next lesson.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nEncourage learners to look out for each other and correct each other while they are in school.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: CHRISTIAN VALUES\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: Working at home\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be able to develop a sense of responsibility of doing chores at homes.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy should you not ask for a reward after working at home?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Citizenship\n Critical thinking and\nproblem solving\n Imagination and\ncreativity\n Unity\n Responsibility\n Concern\n Hard work\n Love\n Social justice\nDecision making\nEmpathy\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nGood news bible.\nCharts with the verse (Philippians 2:4) written on it.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 87-89.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Call the attention of the learners to the key inquiry questions.\nStep 2: Ask learners whether it is good to work at home.\nStep 3: Direct learners to activity 5. Let them look at the picture then lead them to answer the question that follow.\nStep 4: Remind the learners about Philippians 2:4. Learners to recite it as a way of gauging whether they carried out\nthe task.\nStep 5: Ask learners if it is fair/caring about others if they ask for reward for doing work at home. Guide learners to\nsee that it is a show of responsibility if they help with chores at home without expecting a reward.\nStep 6: Direct learners to activity 6 and learners to do Exercise 4.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read summary notes.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer question and inform them of the next lesson.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nEncourage learners to look out for each other and correct each other while they are in school.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS", "ocrText": "", "imageOcrText": "", "imageCount": 0}
{"id": "b9afa345216dc63b", "path": "lesson-plans/General/LESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES (3).docx", "title": "LESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES", "area": "lesson-plans", "level": "General", "format": "docx", "pages": null, "words": 5844, "text": "pener Download The holy Bible a href https drive google com uc export\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE HOLY BIBLE\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: The difference between the Bible and other books.\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to differentiate the bible from other books as a holy book used by\nChristians.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhat is the bible?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Imagination and\ncreativity\n Cooperation\n Holiness\n Respect, responsibility\nInterpersonal relationships\nEffective communication\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nChildren’s bible.\nOther books.\nGood news bible.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 20-21.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Direct learners to page 20 of the learner’s book. Allow them to look at the picture before taking them\nthrough the questions on page 21.\nStep 2: Display the two bible and other books and ask the learners to identify the Bible.\nStep 3: Ask the learners to explain why the bible is special.\nStep 4: Lead learners to sing the song. Encourage them to dramatize.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read out summary notes to complete the explanation\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer questions.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to read summary notes with family members.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE HOLY BIBLE\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: The people who wrote the Bible\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to able to explain how the writing of the bible was different from other\nbooks and respect it.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWho wrote the bible?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Learning to learn\n Cooperation\n Holiness\n Respect, responsibility\nEffective communication\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nPictures of the first pages of the bible.\nGood news bible.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 20-21.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Guide learners to read 2 Timothy 3:16 .\nStep 2: Ask learners what they understand from the Bible verse. Lead them to conclude that the bible was written\nby people who were guided by God.\nStep 3: Guide learners in pairs or groups to do activity 3.\nStep 4: Ask learners to say what they feel about the Bible.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read out summary notes to complete the explanation\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer questions.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to read summary notes with family members.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE HOLY BIBLE\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: Books of the New Testament\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to:-\na. State the number of books in the New Testament and develop interest to read them.\nb. Name the four Gospel books in the New Testament and relate them to the teaching of Jesus Christ.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nHow many books are in the New Testament?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Learning to learn\n Cooperation\nEffective communication\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nFlash cards with names of books of the New Testament.\nGood news bible.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 23-24.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Guide learners to read 2 Timothy 3:16\nStep 2: Ask learners what they understand from the Bible verse. Lead them to conclude that the bible was written\nby many people\nStep 3: Guide learners in pairs or groups to do activity 5.\nStep 4: Encourage the learners to read the Gospel books with the assistance of parents or other adults.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read out summary notes to complete the explanation\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer questions.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to read summary notes with family members.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE HOLY BIBLE\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: It is good to read the Bible\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to appreciate the Bible as a guide in their daily lives.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nHow many books are in the New Testament?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Learning to learn\n Imagination and\ncreativity\n Cooperation\n Responsibility\nEffective communication\nAssertiveness\nDecision making\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nFlash cards with the words of Psalms 119:105.\nManila paper, crayons\nGood news bible.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 24-25.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Guide learners to read Psalms 119:105\nStep 2: Ask learners what they understand from the Bible verse and ask the learners to recite the verse.\nStep 3: Guide learners in pairs or groups to do activity 7.\nStep 4: Encourage the learners to understand the importance of reading the bible.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read out summary notes to complete the explanation\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer questions.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to attend a Bible club if the school has one and participate in the activities.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE HOLY BIBLE\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: The story of Moses and the burning bush\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to narrate what happened in the story of Moses and the burning bush and\nrelate it with the Holy places of worship.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhat happened to Moses at Mount Sinai?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Learning to learn\n Digital literacy\n Obedience\n Responsibility\n Humility\n Holiness\nEffective communication\nAssertiveness\nDecision making\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nVideo of Moses and the burning bush.\nLaptop, a projector.\nGood news bible.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 26-28.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Ask learners question of Activity 1.\nStep 2: Guide learners to look at the pictures then attempt to answer questions that follow.\nStep 3: Guide learners in pairs or groups to read Exodus 3:1-6.\nStep 4: Narrate/read the story from the bible as they follow the picture sequence in the learner’s book.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read out summary notes to complete the explanation.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer questions.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to attend a Bible club if the school has one and participate in the activities.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE HOLY BIBLE\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: The story of Moses and the burning bush\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to narrate what happened in the story of Moses and the burning bush and\nrelate it with the Holy places of worship.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhat happened to Moses at Mount Sinai?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Learning to learn\n Digital literacy\n Obedience\n Responsibility\n Humility\n Holiness\nEffective communication\nAssertiveness\nDecision making\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nVideo of Moses and the burning bush.\nLaptop, a projector.\nGood news bible.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 26-28.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Direct learners through activity 2 and let them say what they like about the story of Moses and the burning\nbush.\nStep 2: Guide learners to watch the video of Moses and the burning bush.\nStep 3: Using questions, guide learners to explain what they saw in the video, in regard to showing respect to holy\nground.\nStep 4: Ask learners to mention Christian holy places. Get learners to commit to respect holy places and have\nhumility in such places.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read out summary notes to complete the explanation\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer questions.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to attend a Bible club if the school has one and participate in the activities.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE HOLY BIBLE\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: The story of Moses and the burning bush.\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to narrate what happened in the story of Moses and the burning bush and\nrelate it with the Holy places of worship.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhat happened to Moses at Mount Sinai?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Learning to learn\n Digital literacy\n Obedience\n Responsibility\n Humility\n Holiness\nEffective communication\nAssertiveness\nDecision making\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nVideo of Moses and the burning bush.\nLaptop, a projector.\nGood news bible.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 26-28.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Direct learners through activity 3.\nStep 2: Guide learners to read Exodus 5-6.\nStep 3: Using questions, guide learners to explain how Moses showed respect to the holy ground.\nStep 4: Ask learners to mention how they will show respect to holy places. Learners to commit to respect holy\nplaces and have humility in such places.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read out summary notes to complete the explanation\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer questions.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to attend a Bible club if the school has one and participate in the activities.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE HOLY BIBLE\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: Moses obeyed God\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to discuss how Moses expressed obedience and apply it in their lives\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nHow did Moses show obedience to God?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Learning to learn\n Imagination and\ncreativity\n Obedience\nInterpersonal relationships\nDecision making\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nProps and costumes for the role play.\nGood news bible.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 29-30.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Direct learners through activity 5 and ask learners what they do when they are called.\nStep 2: Guide learners to read Exodus 3:1-6.\nStep 3: Guide learners to role play the story of Moses.\nStep 4: Ask learners to point out how Moses showed obedience to God in the story. Put the learners in group and\nask them to discuss the question in activity 6.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read out summary notes to complete the explanation\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer questions.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to practice keeping each other accountable when it comes to being obedient..\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE HOLY BIBLE\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: The story of Jonah and the big fish\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to narrate the story of Jonah and be obedient to God.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nHow did Jonah disobey God? What was the result of Jonah’s disobedience?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Learning to learn\n Imagination and\ncreativity\n Obedience\n  Respect\n Forgiveness\n Responsibility\nEffective communication\nDecision making\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nGood news bible.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 31-33.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Direct learners through activity 1 and ask learners the questions.\nStep 2: Guide learners to the pictures under activity 1 and lead them through looking at the pictures and reading\ntext.\nStep 3: Guide learners to read Jonah 1:1-4, 15, 17; 2:10.\nStep 4: Direct learners through activity 2 and ask them to narrate the story of Jonah.\nSUMMARY\nLead learners to appreciate the miracle of Jonah being swallowed and spit out unarmed, by the fish.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer questions.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to practice making a fish mosaic of obedience.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE HOLY BIBLE\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: The story of Jonah and the big fish\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to narrate the story of Jonah and be obedient to God.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nHow did Jonah disobey God? What was the result of Jonah’s disobedience?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Learning to learn\n Imagination and\ncreativity\n Obedience\n  Respect\n Forgiveness\n Responsibility\nEffective communication\nDecision making\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nGood news bible.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 31-33.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Guide learners to read the story from the bible.\nStep 2: Guide learners to role play the story of Jonah.\nSUMMARY\nLead learners to appreciate the miracle of Jonah being swallowed and spit out unarmed, by the fish.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nSummarize the story of Jonah and the big fish.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to practice making a fish mosaic of obedience.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE HOLY BIBLE\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: Jonah is punished by God\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to explain the results of Jonah’s disobedience and desire to obey God.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhat happened to Jonah when he disobeyed God?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Learning to learn\n Imagination and\ncreativity\n Obedience\n  Respect\n Forgiveness\n Responsibility\n Love\nEffective communication\nDecision making\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nGood news bible.\nPapers on which are written scenarios where children were obedient and others disobedient to God, their parents and\ntheir teachers.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 33-34.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Ask learners to say what happens when they disobey. Guide them to do activity 3 on page 33.\nStep 2: Guide learners to read Jonah 1:4, 15, 17\nStep 3: Ask learners to try and explain how Jonah disobeyed God and what happened he disobeyed\nStep 4: Lead the learners to identify the lesson they learn from the disobedience of Jonah and its consequences\nStep 5: Learners should make commitment to forgive others just as God forgave Jonah.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read summary notes.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer questions.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to practice making a fish mosaic of obedience.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE HOLY BIBLE\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: Jonah is punished by God\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to explain the results of Jonah’s disobedience and desire to obey God.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhat happened to Jonah when he disobeyed God?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Learning to learn\n Imagination and\ncreativity\n Obedience\n  Respect\n Forgiveness\n Responsibility\n Love\nEffective communication\nDecision making\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nGood news bible.\nPapers on which are written scenarios where children were obedient and others disobedient to God, their parents and\ntheir teachers.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 33-34.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Ask learners to say what happens when they disobey. Guide them to do activity 3 on page 33.\nStep 2: Guide learners to realize that they can be punished or bad things could happen to them if they disobey God,\ntheir parents and teachers.\nStep 3: Caution learners that they should only obey if what they are told to do is the right thing\nStep 4: Lead learners through scenarios you prepared and observe if they can tell who was obedient and who wasn’t\nStep 5: Guide the learners to activity 4.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read summary notes.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer questions and explain the take home activity\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to practice making a fish mosaic of obedience.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE HOLY BIBLE\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: The story of How Naaman was healed\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to describe the healing of Naaman and desire to have faith in God.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhat happened to Jonah when he disobeyed God?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Learning to learn\n Imagination and\ncreativity\n Obedience\n  Humility\n Faith\n persistence\nEffective communication\nDecision making\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nGood news bible.\nProps and costumes for the role-play.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 35-36.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Introduce the lesson by asking learners to name different diseases they know by asking them the first\nactivity in Activity.\nStep 2: Ask learners to look at the pictures and read the words in the pictures in part 2 of activity 1.\nStep 3: Guide learners to read 2 Kings 5:1-14\nStep 4: Using questions guide the learners to understand that Naaman was healed because he had faith In God and\nbecause he followed instructions.\nStep 5: Ask learners what they learn from the story and how they will apply what they have learned.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read summary notes.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer questions and explain the take home activity\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to participate in health programmes in the school.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE HOLY BIBLE\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: The story of How Naaman was healed\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to describe the healing of Naaman and desire to have faith in God.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhat happened to Jonah when he disobeyed God?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Learning to learn\n Imagination and\ncreativity\n Obedience\n  Humility\n Faith\n persistence\nEffective communication\nDecision making\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nGood news bible.\nProps and costumes for the role-play.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 35-36.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Introduce the lesson by asking learners to name the disease Naaman was suffering from.\nStep 2: Ask learners to read 2 Kings 5:1-14 in turns.\nStep 3: Explain to the learners that Naaman had faith and followed instructions and that is why he got healed.\nStep 4: Direct learners through activity 3 and guide learners to role play the story using props and costumes you\nprepared.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read summary notes.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer questions and explain the take home activity\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to participate in health programmes in the school.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE HOLY BIBLE\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: God heals us\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to appreciate God as the healer of all diseases.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWho heals you when you are sick?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Learning to learn\n Obedience\n  Humility\n Faith\n Persistence\n Social justice\nEffective communication\nDecision making\nSelf-esteem\nHealth education\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nGood news bible.\nMirrors or other reflective surfaces.\nA chart showing different people being treated in hospital\nLearner’s Book 3 page 36-37.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Direct learners to activity 4 in the learner’s book page 36.\nStep 2: Ask learners if they have ever been in unwell and what happened so that they could get better.\nStep 3: Lead learners to the understanding that it is God who ultimately healed Naaman. Elisha was used by God to\nheal Naaman.\nStep 4: Through questions, lead learners to commit to have faith in God to heal them when they are unwell. Ask\nthem how they can show this faith.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read summary notes.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nReview the lesson\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to participate in health programmes in the school.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE HOLY BIBLE\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: God heals us\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to appreciate God as the healer of all diseases.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWho heals you when you are sick?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Learning to learn\n Obedience\n  Humility\n Faith\n Persistence\n Social justice\nEffective communication\nDecision making\nSelf-esteem\nHealth education\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nGood news bible.\nMirrors or other reflective surfaces.\nA chart showing different people being treated in hospital.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 36-37.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Review the questions on what learners do when they are sick.\nStep 2: Through questions, remind the learners of the story of how Naaman was healed.\nStep 3: Ask learners what they think would have happened if Naaman had not followed instructions\nStep 4: Guide to do activity 5 and guide them to committing that they will have faith in God and will follow the\ndoctor’s instructions in order to get healed.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read summary notes.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer question and describe the take home activity.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to participate in health programmes in the school.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE HOLY BIBLE\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: The story of the three Hebrew men\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to narrate the story of the three Hebrew men and strengthen their\nrelationship with God.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhat happened to the three Hebrew men? Who rescued the three Hebrew men from fire?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Learning to learn\n Imagination and\ncreativity\n Trust\n Faith\n Courage\nEffective communication\nDecision making\nassertiveness\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nGood news bible.\nLaptop, projector, video of the story.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 38-39.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Ask learners to name the various local communities In Kenya that they know.\nStep 2: Direct learners to questions 1 in activity 1.\nStep 3: Point learners to part 2 of activity 1. Give them time to look at the pictures\nStep 4: Guide to read the bibles verses and lead them realization that the three Hebrew men refused to worship a\nstatue and were thrown into the fire.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read summary notes.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to sing a song that covers the story of the three Hebrew men.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to participate in a fire drill for the whole school.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE HOLY BIBLE\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: The story of the three Hebrew men\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to narrate the story of the three Hebrew men and strengthen their\nrelationship with God.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhat happened to the three Hebrew men? Who rescued the three Hebrew men from fire?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Learning to learn\n Imagination and\ncreativity\n Trust\n Faith\n Courage\nEffective communication\nDecision making\nassertiveness\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nGood news bible.\nLaptop, projector, video of the story.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 38-39.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Guide learners to watch a video of the three Hebrew boys.\nStep 2: Let learners to state the lessons they learn from the story and explain how they will apply them in their\nlives.\nStep 3: Ask learners questions to evaluate how well they have understood the key details of the story.\nStep 4: Guide learners to have faith and trust in God in their own lives.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read summary notes.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to sing a song that covers the story of the three Hebrew men.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to participate in a fire drill for the whole school.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTHREE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE HOLY BIBLE\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: The story of the three Hebrew men\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to trust God to cope with daily challenges.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy should I trust God?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Learning to learn\n Imagination and\ncreativity\n Self-efficacy\n Trust\n Faith\n Courage\n responsibility\nEffective communication\nDecision making\nassertiveness\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nGood news bible.\nFlash cards with situations that require assertiveness, and others requiring trust and faith in God.\nLearner’s Book 3 page 40-41.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nReview the previous lesson.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Ask learners if someone has ever told them to do a bad thing.\nStep 2: Direct learners to activity 3 and ask them to answer the questions.\nStep 3: Guide learners to find and read Daniel 3:15-16, 18.\nStep 4: Guide learners to realize that what the three Hebrew did is assertiveness that is speaking without fear.\nStep 5: Guide learners in pairs or groups to discuss situations on flash cards. Ask learners to do activity 4 in pairs as\nyou supervise them.\nSUMMARY\nLearners to read summary notes.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask 