tencies Values PCIs\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Responsibility\nEnvironmental education\nCitizenship\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nA video clip showing animals feeding\nPhotographs showing different types of animals kept at home\nEnrich Yourself Environmental activities Teachers guide pg.89\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs/groups\nINTRODUCTION\nDo a brainstorming activity with learners\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Learners to review their visit to the animal farm and in groups discuss how they feed and water animals.\nStep 2: Learners to share and discuss different experiences about feeding and watering animals at home.\nStep 3: Guide learners to practice feeding and watering animals at home.\nStep 4: Learners to observe safety measures.\nSUMMARY\nMake summary points/notes\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and ask questions.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to talk to their parents/guardians on equipment for feeding and watering animals at home.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN ENVIRONMENTAL ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nONE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: CARE FOR THE ENVIRONMENT\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: Caring for animals- Cleaning the equipment for feeding and\nwatering animals\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be able to identify common feeds for various domestic animals.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\n What do domestic animals eat?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Responsibility\nEnvironmental education\nCitizenship\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nA video clip showing animals feeding\nPhotographs showing different types of animals kept at home\nEnrich Yourself Environmental activities Teachers guide pg.90\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs/groups\nINTRODUCTION\nDo a brainstorming activity with learners\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Learners to review their visit to the animal farm and in groups discuss how they feed and water animals.(can\nbe done virtually)\nStep 2: Learners to take photos of the equipment used and how they are cleaned\nStep 3: Ask learners to observe the type of diet of the animals, ratio of food and times of feeding\nStep 4: In the classroom learners to observe pictures taken and to watch a video of the cleaning process. Learners to\ndo activity on page 42\nSUMMARY\nMake summary points/notes\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and ask questions.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to talk to their parents/guardians on cleaning equipment for feeding and watering animals at home.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN ENVIRONMENTAL ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nONE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: CARE FOR THE ENVIRONMENT\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: Managing waste responsibly- types of waste in a classroom\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be able to\n Identify types of waste in the classroom\n Safely sort out waste in the classroom for appropriate disposal\n Dispose of waste responsibly to limit risk to self, others and environment.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\n What types of waste are found in the classroom?\n How can we dispose of classroom waste responsibly?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Responsibility\nEnvironmental education\nCitizenship\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nSamples of type of waste\nChart illustrating different types of waste\nPencils, crayons and drawing books\nPictures of common things used in handling waste e.g. broom, dust pan, gloves\nSlogan on recycling\nEnrich Yourself Environmental activities Teachers guide pg.92-94\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs/groups\nINTRODUCTION\nDo a brainstorming activity with learners\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Ask learners to move around the class and i