 protective gear and collect waste found in the classroom\nStep 4: Guide learners to identify the various types of waste in the class and guide them through activity on page 43\nSUMMARY\nMake summary points/notes\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to discuss among themselves about types of waste they have collected\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to draw and colour different types of waste in their classroom.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN ENVIRONMENTAL ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nONE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: CARE FOR THE ENVIRONMENT\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: Managing waste responsibly- Things used in handling waste\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be able to\n Identify types of waste in the classroom\n Safely sort out waste in the classroom for appropriate disposal\n Dispose of waste responsibly to limit risk to self, others and environment.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\n What types of waste are found in the classroom?\n How can we dispose of classroom waste responsibly?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Responsibility\nEnvironmental education\nCitizenship\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nSamples of type of waste\nChart illustrating different types of waste\nPencils, crayons and drawing books\nPictures of common things used in handling waste e.g. broom, dust pan, gloves\nSlogan on recycling\nEnrich Yourself Environmental activities Teachers guide pg.94-95\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs/groups\nINTRODUCTION\nDo a brainstorming activity with learners\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Ask learners to move around the class and identify any litter on the floor, window panes.\nStep 2: Guide learners on the correct ways of cleaning and sorting waste.\nStep 3: After the activity learners to describe their experiences and what they have learnt about waste collection.\nStep 4: Learners to view pictures and drawings that show things used to handle waste in the classroom.\nSUMMARY\nLearner to sing a song about cleanliness\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to draw and colour out some of the things they use to handle waste in their classroom\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to draw and colour different types of waste in their classroom.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN ENVIRONMENTAL ACTIVITIES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nONE\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: CARE FOR THE ENVIRONMENT\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: Managing waste responsibly- Sorting waste safely for appropriate\ndisposal\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be able to\n Identify types of waste in the classroom\n Safely sort out waste in the classroom for appropriate disposal\n Dispose of waste responsibly to limit risk to self, others and environment.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\n What types of waste are found in the classroom?\n How can we dispose of classroom waste responsibly?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Communication and\ncollaboration\n Responsibility\nEnvironmental education\nCitizenship\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nSamples of type of waste\nChart illustrating different types of waste\nPencils, crayons and drawing books\nPictures of common things used in handling waste e.g. broom, dust pan, gloves\nSlogan on recycling\nEnrich Yourself Environmental activities Teachers guide pg.95-96\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs/groups\nINTRODUCTION\nDo a brainstorming activity with learners\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Ask learners to move around the class and identify any litter on the floor, window panes.\nStep 2: Guide learners on wearing protective gear\nStep 3: Guide learner to collect waste in the class and prepare it for safe disposal.\nStep 4: Guide learners to sort out the waste according to category.\nStep 5: Guide learners to classify the waste on page 4