all of Samuel.\nSUMMARY\nReview the lesson.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to recite 1 Samuel 3:3-11.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to visit a church and listen to the Bible story on the call of Samuel.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE HOLY BIBLE\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: THE CALL OF SAMUEL\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to describe the call of Samuel and relate it to their lives by obeying\nGod.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhat do you do when God calls you?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Friendship formation\n Responsibility\n Respect\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nCritical thinking\ncitizenship\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible.\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 37-41.\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 22-24.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song on the call of Samuel.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Guide learners to read the Bible story of the call of Samuel from 1Samuel 3:3-11.\nStep 2: Guide learners in watching a video with the story of the call of Samuel.\nStep 3: Learners to role play the call of Samuel as a way of knowing the importance of being obedient both to\nGod and the people around us.\nStep 4: Learners to sing a simple song about the call of Samuel.\nSUMMARY\nSamuel was called by God.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to recite 1 Samuel 3:10\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to visit a church and listen to the Bible story on the call of Samuel.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE HOLY BIBLE\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: THE CALL OF SAMUEL\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to desire to respond appropriately to God by obeying His word.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhat do you do when God calls you?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Friendship formation\n Responsibility\n Respect\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nCritical thinking\ncitizenship\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible.\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 37-41.\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 22-24\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song on the call of Samuel.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Guide learners to read the Bible story of the call of Samuel from 1Samuel 3:3-11.\nStep 2: Guide learners in watching a video with the story of the call of Samuel.\nStep 3: Learners to Learn to obey God by reading the Bible and doing what it tells them to do.\nStep 4: Learners to show desire in responding to Gods call despite being young.\nSUMMARY\nReview the lesson and make summary.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to recite 1 Samuel 3:10\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to visit a church and listen to the Bible story on the call of Samuel.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE HOLY BIBLE\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: NOAH AND THE ARK\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to state the reason why God chose Noah to build the ark and live a\nlife that is pleasing to God.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy should we obey God?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Responsibility\n Respect\n Obedience\n Care and love\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nCritical thinking\ncitizenship\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible.\nVideo clips.\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 42-49.\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 25-28.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song on Noah and the Ark.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Explain to the learners on the importance of being obedient and od-fearing in relation to the Biblical\naccount of Noah.\nStep 2: Guide learners in watching a video with the story of Noah and the Ark.\nStep 3: Learners to role play in small groups the story of Noah and the Ark.\nSUMMARY\nNoah and his family built the ark.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to Read Genesis 6:9-10\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to visit a church elder and listen to the Bible story of Noah and the Ark.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE HOLY BIBLE\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: NOAH AND THE ARK\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to state the reason why God chose Noah to build the ark and live a\nlife that is pleasing to God.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy should we obey God?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Responsibility\n Respect\n Obedience\n Care and love\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nCritical thinking\ncitizenship\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible.\nVideo clips.\nPieces of paper.\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 42-49.\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 25-28\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song on Noah and the Ark.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Explain to the learners on the importance of being obedient and od-fearing in relation to the Biblical\naccount of Noah.\nStep 2: Guide learners in watching a video with the story of Noah and the Ark.\nStep 3: Guide learners in making paper boats\nStep 4: Learners to draw and colour a boat floating on water.\nSUMMARY\nReview the lesson and make summary.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to Read Genesis 6:9-10\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to visit a church elder and listen to the Bible story of Noah and the Ark.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE HOLY BIBLE\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: NOAH AND THE ARK\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to state the reason why God chose Noah to build the ark and live a\nlife that is pleasing to God.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy should we obey God?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Responsibility\n Respect\n Obedience\n Care and love\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nCritical thinking\ncitizenship\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible.\nVideo clips\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 42-49.\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 25-28.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song on Noah and the Ark.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Explain to the learners on the importance of being obedient and od-fearing in relation to the Biblical\naccount of Noah.\nStep 2: Guide learners in watching a video with the story of Noah and the Ark.\nStep 3: Learners to sing the song “the animals went in two by two”\nStep 4: Learners to discuss in groups why they should obey God.\nSUMMARY\nWe should be obedient to God.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to Read Genesis 6:9-10\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to visit a church elder and listen to the Bible story of Noah and the Ark.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nS