eem\nCritical thinking\ncitizenship\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible.\nVideo clips.\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 50-56.\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 29-31.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song on about Daniel.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Learners to Read the story of Daniel in the lion’s Den in Daniel 6:10-12, 19-22.\nStep 2: Discuss with the learners the importance prayer in the case of Daniel.\nStep 3: Learners to mention how many times Daniel Prayed.\nSUMMARY\nLearners should strive to be like Daniel.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to recite Daniel 6:10-12\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to participate in church activities that will strengthen their trust in God.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE HOLY BIBLE\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: THE STORY OF DANIEL\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to mention the number of times Daniel prayed to God and relate it to\ntheir lives.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy is prayer important?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Faith\n Patience\n Courage and trust\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nCritical thinking\ncitizenship\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible.\nVideo clips\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 50-56.\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 29-31.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song on about Daniel.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Learners to Read the story of Daniel in the lion’s Den in Daniel 6:10-12, 19-22.\nStep 2: Learners to watch a video on the story of Daniel in the Den of Lions.\nStep 3: Learners to sing the song on “Trust and obey for there is no other way”.\nSUMMARY\nWe should trust God\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to recite Daniel 6:10-12\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to participate in church activities that will strengthen their trust in God.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE HOLY BIBLE\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: THE STORY OF DANIEL\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to acquire the skill of assertiveness by emulating Daniel in their\nlives.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy is the importance of being courageous?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Faith\n Patience\n Courage and trust\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nCritical thinking\ncitizenship\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible.\nVideo clips.\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 50-56.\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 29-31.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song on about Daniel.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Learners to Read the story of Daniel in the lion’s Den in Daniel 6:10-12, 19-22.\nStep 2: Learners to watch a video on the story of Daniel in the Den of Lions.\nStep 3: Learners to role play Daniel in the Den of lions and how he was rescued.\nStep 4: Learners to model a lion.\nSUMMARY\nReview the lesson and make summary\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to recite Daniel 6:10-12\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to participate in church activities that will strengthen their trust in God.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSUBSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE HOLY BIBLE\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: THE STORY OF DANIEL\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to acquire the skill of assertiveness by emulating Daniel in their lives\nand appreciate God as the protector by trusting him.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy is the importance of being courageous?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Faith\n Patience\n Courage and trust\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nCritical thinking\ncitizenship\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible.\nVideo clips\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 50-56.\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 29-31.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song on about Daniel.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Learners to Read the story of Daniel in the lion’s Den in Daniel 6:10-12, 19-22.\nStep 2: Learners to watch a video on the story of Daniel in the Den of Lions.\nStep 3: Learners to role play Daniel in the Den of lions and how he was rescued.\nStep 4: Learners to discuss how to be assertive in life.\nSUMMARY\nWe should be bold each time.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to recite Daniel 6:10-12\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to participate in church activities that will strengthen their trust in God.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE HOLY BIBLE\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: THE WIDOW OF ZAREPHATH\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to narrate the story of the widow of Zarephath and trust God for their\nneeds.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy should trust God for providence?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Faith\n Sharing\n Concern and love\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nCritical thinking\ncitizenship\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible.\nVideo clips.\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 57-60.\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 31-34.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song on Elijah.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning).\nStep 1: Learners to Read the story in 1 Kings 17:7-16.\nStep 2: Explain to the learners the importance of trusting and having unwavering faith in God in relation to the\nstory Read.\nStep 3: Learners to narrate the story.\nStep 4: Ask learners what they have learnt from the story.\nSUMMARY\nWe should share with the less fortunate.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to read 1kings 17:7-16.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to visit with their parents families around and are less fortunate to share with them.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE HOLY BIBLE\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: THE WIDOW OF ZAREPHATH\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to narrate the story of the widow of Zarephath and trust God for their\nneeds.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy should trust God for providence?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Faith\n Sharing\n Concern and love\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nCritical thinking\ncitizenship\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible.\nVideo clips.\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 57-60.\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 31-34.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song on Elijah.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Learners to Read the story in 1 Kings 17:7-16.\nStep 2: Explain to the learners the importance of trusting and having unwavering faith in God in relation to the\nstory Read.\nStep 3: Learners to role play the story of Elijah and the widow of Zarephath.\nStep 4: Learners to sing a song about trusting in God.\nSUMMARY\nReview the lesson and make summary.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to read 1kings 17:7-16\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to visit with their parents families around and are less fortunate to share with them.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE HOLY BIBLE\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: THE WIDOW OF ZAREPHATH\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to narrate the story of the widow of Zarephath and trust God for their\nneeds.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy should trust God for providence?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Faith\n Sharing\n Concern and love\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nCritical thinking\ncitizenship\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible.\nVideo clips.\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 57-60.\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 31-34.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song on Elijah.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Learners to Read the story in 1 Kings 17:7-16.\nStep 2: Explain to the learners the importance of trusting and having unwavering faith in God in relation to the\nstory Read.\nStep 3: Learners to draw and colour a loaf of bread.\nStep 4: Guide the learners through the activities in the learner’s book.\nSUMMARY\nReview the lesson and make summary.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to read 1kings 17:7-16\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to visit with their parents families around and are less fortunate to share with them.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE HOLY BIBLE\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: THE WIDOW OF ZAREPHATH\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to appreciate in the miracle of multiplication of flour and oil and\nhave faith in Him as the provider.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy should trust God for providence?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Faith\n Sharing\n Concern and love\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nCritical thinking\ncitizenship\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible.\nVideo clips.\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 57-60.\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 31-34.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song on Elijah.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Learners to Read the story in 1 Kings 17:7-16\nStep 2: Learners to narrate the story of multiplication of flour and oil.\nStep 3: Learners to express willingness to share whatever little they have.\nStep 4: Learners to sing a song about trusting in God.\nSUMMARY\nWe should be kind to each other.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to read 1kings 17:7-16\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to visit with their parents families around and are less fortunate to share with them.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS", "ocrText": "", "imageOcrText": "", "imageCount": 0}
{"id": "e504b10c3212e562", "path": "lesson-plans/Grade 2/LESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES (4).docx", "title": "LESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES", "area": "lesson-plans", "level": "Grade 2", "format": "docx", "pages": null, "words": 1996, "text": "noopener Download The Church a href https drive google com uc export d\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE CHURCH\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: PRAYER\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to recite the first 4 lines of the Lord’s pray as a way of communicating\nto God.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nHow do we pray?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Trust\n Humility\n Faith and hope\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible.\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 101-104.\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 62-64.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Learners to read Matthew 6:9-10.\nStep 2: Guide learners to recite the first 4 lines of the Lord’s Prayer.\nStep 3: Encourage learners to pray/say simple prayers.\nSUMMARY\nWe should pray always.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to recite the Lord’s Prayer\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to participate in prayers during school assemblies and participate in bible in club activities.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE CHURCH\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: PRAYER\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to recite the first 4 lines of the Lord’s pray as a way of communicating\nto God.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nHow do we pray?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Trust\n Humility\n Faith and hope\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible.\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 101-104.\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 62-64.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Learners to read Matthew 6:9-10\nStep 2: Guide learners to recite the first 4 lines of the Lord’s Prayer.\nStep 3: Encourage learners to pray/say simple prayers.\nStep 4: Guide learners on the importance of prayer.\nSUMMARY\nWe should pray always.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to recite the Lord’s Prayer\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to participate in prayers during school assemblies and participate in bible in club activities.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE CHURCH\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: PRAYER\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to narrate the story of a friend at midnight and apply it in their lives.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nHow do we pray?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Trust\n Humility\n Faith and hope\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible.\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 101-104.\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 62-64.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Learners to read Luke 11:5-10.\nStep 2: Guide learners to read the story of a friend at midnight. The story puts emphasis on faith in God during\nprayers.\nStep 3: Guide learners in groups or pairs to discuss the importance of prayer.\nSUMMARY\nWe should pray always.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to recite the Lord’s Prayer\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to participate in prayers during school assemblies and participate in bible in club activities.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE CHURCH\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: PRAYER\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to narrate the story of a friend at midnight and apply it in their lives and\ndesire to pray regularly.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nHow do we pray?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Trust\n Humility\n Faith and hope\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible.\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 101-104.\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 62-64.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Learners to read Luke 11:5-10.\nStep 2: Guide learners to read the story of a friend at midnight. The story puts emphasis on faith in God during\nprayers.\nStep 3: Guide learners in groups or pairs to discuss the importance of prayer.\nStep 4: Guide learners to role-play the story of a friend at midnight.\nSUMMARY\nReview the lesson and make summary.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to recite the Lord’s Prayer\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to participate in prayers during school assemblies and participate in bible in club activities.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE CHURCH\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: THE HOLY SPIRIT\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to state the promises Jesus gave to his disciples, and desire to have faith\nin God.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhat are the works of the Holy Spirit on your life?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Hope\n Unity\n Courage\n love\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible.\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 105-108.\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 64-66.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song .\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Learners to read Acts 1:4 and Acts 2:3-4.\nStep 2: Explain to the learners the term “promise” using the conversation between Mark and his parents on page\n105 of the learner’s book.\nStep 3: Describe Jesus promise of a helper to the believers.\nStep 4: Explain the work of the Holy Spirit to the learners.\nSUMMARY\nReview the lesson and make summary.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer questions.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to sing a song about the work of the Holy Spirit.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE CHURCH\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: THE HOLY SPIRIT\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to state the promises Jesus gave to his disciples, and desire to have faith\nin God.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhat are the works of the Holy Spirit on your life?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Hope\n Unity\n Courage\n love\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible.\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 105-108.\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 64-66.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Learners to read Acts 1:4 and Acts 2:3-4.\nStep 2: Explain to the learners the term “promise” using the conversation between Mark and his parents on page\n105 of the learner’s book.\nStep 3: Guide learners in groups or pairs to list the work of the Holy Spirit in the lives.\nSUMMARY\nReview the lesson and make summary.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer questions.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to sing a song about the work of the Holy Spirit.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE CHURCH\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: THE HOLY SPIRIT\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to state the promises Jesus gave to his disciples, and desire to have faith\nin God.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhat are the works of the Holy Spirit on your life?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Hope\n Unity\n Courage\n love\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible.\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 105-108.\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 64-66.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Learners to read Acts 1:4 and Acts 2:3-4.\nStep 2: Explain to the learners the term “promise” using the conversation between Mark and his parents on page\n105 of the learner’s book.\nStep 3: Guide learners in groups or pairs to list the work of the Holy Spirit in the lives.\nStep 4: Guide learners to write the work of the Holy Spirit on flash cards and read them aloud in pairs.\nSUMMARY\nReview the lesson and make summary\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer questions.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to sing a song about the work of the Holy Spirit.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE CHURCH\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: THE HOLY SPIRIT\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to state the promises Jesus gave to his disciples, and desire to have faith\nin God.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhat are the works of the Holy Spirit on your life?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Hope\n Unity\n Courage\n love\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible.\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 105-108.\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 64-66.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Learners to read Acts 1:4 and Acts 2:3-4.\nStep 2: Explain to the learners the term “promise” using the conversation between Mark and his parents on page\n105 of the learner’s book.\nStep 3: Guide learners in groups or pairs to list the work of the Holy Spirit in the lives.\nStep 4: Guide learners to sing a song about the work of the Holy Spirit.\nSUMMARY\nWe should believe the promises of Jesus Christ.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer questions.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to sing a song about the work of the Holy Spirit.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE CHURCH\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: THE HOLY SPIRIT\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to state the promises Jesus gave to his disciples, and desire to have faith\nin God and appreciate the work of Holy Spirit in their day to day lives.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhat are the works of the Holy Spirit on your life?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Hope\n Unity\n Courage\n love\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible.\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 105-108.\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 64-66.\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups.\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song.\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Learners to read Acts 1:4 and Acts 2:3 .\nStep 2: Explain to the learners the term “promise” using the conversation between Mark and his parents on page\n105 of the learner’s book.\nStep 3: Guide learners in groups or pairs to list the work of the Holy Spirit in the lives. (Read Romans 8:14,\nEphesians 4:3-4, Luke 24: 49)\nStep 4: Guide learners to discuss the work of the Holy Spirit in their lives today.\nSUMMARY\nReview the lesson and make summary\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to ask and answer questions.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to sing a song about the work of the Holy Spirit.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS", "ocrText": "", "imageOcrText": "", "imageCount": 0}
{"id": "be4ed4d4ee61aa70", "path": "lesson-plans/Grade 2/LESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES (5).docx", "title": "LESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES", "area": "lesson-plans", "level": "Grade 2", "format": "docx", "pages": null, "words": 5122, "text": "a The early life of Jesus Christ a href https drive google com uc expo\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE EARLY LIFE OF JESUS CHRIST\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: THE KINDNESS OF THE WISEMEN\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to list the gifts given to baby Jesus and develop the value of sharing.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy should we share gifts?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Faith\n Sharing\n Love and unity\n Kindness\n obedience\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible\nVideo clips\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 61-66\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 35-38\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song on baby Jesus\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Learners to Read the story in Mathew 2:11\nStep 2: Guide learners in naming the gifts brought to baby Jesus by the three wise men.\nStep 3: Ask learners the lessons they learn from the three wise men and develop the value of sharing.\nSUMMARY\nWe should be kind.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to recite Mathew 2:11\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to participate in community activities e.g. Christmas time where people give gifts.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE EARLY LIFE OF JESUS CHRIST\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: THE KINDNESS OF THE WISEMEN\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to list the gifts given to baby Jesus and develop the value of sharing.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy should we share gifts?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Faith\n Sharing\n Love and unity\n Kindness\n obedience\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible\nVideo clips\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 61-66\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 35-38\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song on baby Jesus\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Learners to Read the story in Mathew 2:11\nStep 2: Guide learners in naming the gifts brought to baby Jesus by the three wise men.\nStep 3: Guide learners to draw and colour gifts given to baby Jesus.\nStep 4: Learners to sing a gratitude song about Jesus love ‘…Jesus’ love is very wonderful..”.\nSUMMARY\nReview the lesson and make summary\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to recite Mathew 2:11\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to participate in community activities e.g. Christmas time where people give gifts.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE EARLY LIFE OF JESUS CHRIST\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: THE KINDNESS OF THE WISEMEN\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to acquire the skill of assertiveness, by refusing gifts from strangers\nand appreciate Jesus as a gift from God, in their lives.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy should we not receive gifts from strangers?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Faith\n Sharing\n Love and unity\n Kindness\n obedience\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible\nVideo clips\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 61-66\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 35-38\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song on baby Jesus\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Learners to Read the story in Mathew 2:11\nStep 2: Guide learners to role-play saying “thank you”, after receiving gifts from friends and family members\nusing flash cards.\nStep 3: Guide learners to understand why they should avoid receiving gifts from strangers.\nStep 4: Learners to appreciate baby Jesus as a gift from God.\nSUMMARY\nWe should not accept gifts from strangers.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to recite Mathew 2:11\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to participate in community activities e.g. Christmas time where people give gifts.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE EARLY LIFE OF JESUS CHRIST\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: THE KINDNESS OF THE WISEMEN\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to acquire the skill of assertiveness, by refusing gifts from strangers\nand appreciate Jesus as a gift from God, in their lives.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy should we not receive gifts from strangers?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Faith\n Sharing\n Love and unity\n Kindness\n obedience\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible\nVideo clips\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 61-66\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 35-38\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song on baby Jesus\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Learners to Read the story in Mathew 2:11\nStep 2: Guide learners to role-play saying “thank you”, after receiving gifts from friends and family members\nusing flash cards.\nStep 3: Explain to the learners why they should avoid receiving gifts from strangers.\nStep 4: Learners in groups or pairs to list the negative results of receiving gifts from strangers.\nSUMMARY\nWe should not accept gifts from strangers.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to recite Mathew 2:11\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to participate in community activities e.g. Christmas time where people give gifts.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE EARLY LIFE OF JESUS CHRIST\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: JESUS CHRIST WORKED\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to develop responsibility by doing simple chores at home, in school\nand the church.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy should we help our parents/work?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Trust\n Responsibility\n Love\n Obedience\n Humility and respect\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 67-70\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 39-40\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song on baby Jesus\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Explain to the learners the type of work Jesus did at home to help his father Joseph. i.e. carpentry\nStep 2: Guide learners in groups to list how Jesus helped his father.\nStep 3: Learners to write a poem on “Jesus worked”.\nSUMMARY\nReview the lesson and make summary\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to recite the poem\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to participate in different activities or work in the community, interacting and learning from them.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nS