st\n Responsibility\n Love\n Obedience\n Humility and respect\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 67-70\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 39-40\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song on baby Jesus\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Explain to the learners the type of work Jesus did at home to help his father Joseph. i.e. carpentry\nStep 2: Guide learners in groups to list how Jesus helped his father.\nStep 3: Educate learners on how to responsible both at home and in school.\nStep 4: Learners to discuss in groups or in pairs what chores they do at home and in school.\nSUMMARY\nWe should do every work given to us.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to recite the poem\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to participate in different activities or work in the community, interacting and learning from them.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE EARLY LIFE OF JESUS CHRIST\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: JESUS CHRIST WORKED\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to appreciate work by emulating Jesus Christ and assisting their\nparents at home\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy should we help our parents/work?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Trust\n Responsibility\n Love\n Obedience\n Humility and respect\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 67-70\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 39-40\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song on baby Jesus\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Explain to the learners the type of work Jesus did at home to help his father Joseph. I.e. carpentry\nStep 2: Guide learners in groups to list how Jesus helped his father.\nStep 3: Educate learners on how to responsible both at home and in school.\nStep 4: Learners to discuss in groups or in pairs what chores they do at home and in school and emulate the life\nof Jesus in them.\nSUMMARY\nReview the lesson and make summary.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to recite the poem\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to participate in different activities or work in the community, interacting and learning from them.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE EARLY LIFE OF JESUS CHRIST\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: JESUS CALMS THE STORM\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to narrate the miracle of calming the storm and relate it to their daily\nlives by having faith in God.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy should we have faith?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Trust\n Responsibility\n Love\n Obedience\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible\nVideo clip\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 71-72\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 40-42\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song on the calming of storm\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Guide learners to read Matthew 8:23-27\nStep 2: Guide learners in watching a video clip on the miracle of calming the storm.\nStep 3: Learners to sing a song about the calming of the storm..\nSUMMARY\nReview the lesson and make summary.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to sing a song.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to pray with family members.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE EARLY LIFE OF JESUS CHRIST\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: JESUS CALMS THE STORM\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to narrate the miracle of calming the storm and relate it to their daily\nlives by having faith in God.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy should we have faith?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Trust\n Responsibility\n Love\n Obedience\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible\nVideo clip\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 71-72\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 40-42\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song on the calming of storm\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Guide learners to read Matthew 8:23-27\nStep 2: Guide learners in watching a video clip on the miracle of calming the storm.\nStep 3: Guide learners to role play the miracle of calming the storm.\nStep 4: Learners to discuss in pairs what they do when they are facing difficulties.\nSUMMARY\nWe should have faith in Jesus Christ.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to sing a song.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to pray with family members.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE EARLY LIFE OF JESUS CHRIST\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: JESUS CALMS THE STORM\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to narrate the miracle of calming the storm and relate it to their daily\nlives by having faith in God and appreciating the miracle of calming the storm by trusting God when faced with\nchallenges.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy should we have faith?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Trust\n Responsibility\n Love\n Obedience\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible\nVideo clip\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 71-72\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 40-42\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song on the calming of storm\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Guide learners to read Matthew 8:23-27\nStep 2: Guide learners in watching a video clip on the miracle of calming the storm.\nStep 3: Guide learners in drawing and colouring a boat.\nStep 4: Explain to the learners the importance of having faith in God.\nSUMMARY\nReview the lesson and make summary\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to sing a song.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to pray with family members.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE EARLY LIFE OF JESUS CHRIST\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: THE MIRACULOUS CATCH OF FISH\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to explain how Jesus solved the problem of the fishermen, and relate\nit to their lives by trusting in God.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy should we have trust in God?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Faith\n Obedience\n Hard-work\n Cooperation\n Responsibility, love and\ntrust\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible\nVideo clip\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 73-75\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 43-44\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Guide learners to read Luke 5:3-9\nStep 2: Guide learners in watching a video clip on the miraculous catch of fish.\nStep 3: Explain to the learners the importance of having faith in God.\nStep 4: Guide learners in groups or pairs to tell how Jesus solved the problem of the fishermen.\nSUMMARY\nWe should trust in God.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to sing a song.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to take a nature walk and visit a fish pond in the company of parents/guardians.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE EARLY LIFE OF JESUS CHRIST\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: THE MIRACULOUS CATCH OF FISH\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to explain how Jesus solved the problem of the fishermen, and relate\nit to their lives by trusting in God.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy should we have trust in God?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Faith\n Obedience\n Hard-work\n Cooperation\n Responsibility, love and\ntrust\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible\nVideo clip\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 73-75\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 43-44\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Guide learners to read Luke 5:3-9\nStep 2: Guide learners in watching a video clip on the miraculous catch of fish.\nStep 3: Guide learners to role play the miraculous catch of fish.\nStep 4: Learners to sing the song, “I will make you fishers of men”\nSUMMARY\nWe should trust God.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to sing a song.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to take a nature walk and visit a fish pond in the company of parents/guardians.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRA