p on the healing of the man with withered hand.\nStep 3: Guide learners to relate the story in their lives and trust God for healing.\nSUMMARY\nGod heals\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to sing a song.\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to visit the physically challenged in the company of their parents to pray with them and help them with\nhousehold chores..\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE EARLY LIFE OF JESUS CHRIST\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: HEALING OF THE MAN WITH THE WITHERED HAND.\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to describe the healing of the man with a withered hand and relate it\nto their lives, by trusting God for healing.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy should we assist those who are sick?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Compassion\n Love\n Faith\n Social justice and trust\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible\nVideo clip\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 76-77\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 45-46\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Guide learners to read Matthew 12:9-13\nStep 2: Guide learners in watching a video clip on the healing of the man with withered hand.\nStep 3: Guide learners in pairs to draw a withered hand\nStep 4: Guide learners in assisting their friends who are sick and with special needs.\nSUMMARY\nReview the lesson and make summary.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to recite Matthew 12:13\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to visit the physically challenged in the company of their parents to pray with them and help them with\nhousehold chores..\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE EARLY LIFE OF JESUS CHRIST\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: HEALING OF THE MAN WITH THE WITHERED HAND.\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to describe the healing of the man with a withered hand and relate it\nto their lives, by trusting God for healing.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy should we assist those who are sick?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Compassion\n Love\n Faith\n Social justice and trust\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible\nVideo clip\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 76-77\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 45-46\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Guide learners to read Matthew 12:9-13\nStep 2: Guide learners in writing Matthew 12:13 on flash cards and recite it aloud in front of the class.\nStep 3: Learners to describe the healing of the man with withered hand.\nSUMMARY\nReview the lesson and make summary\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to recite Matthew 12:13\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to visit the physically challenged in the company of their parents to pray with them and help them with\nhousehold chores..\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE EARLY LIFE OF JESUS CHRIST\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: HEALING OF THE MAN WITH THE WITHERED HAND.\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to describe the healing of the man with a withered hand and relate it\nto their lives, by trusting God for healing and appreciate Jesus’ compassion, by expressing kindness to others.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy should we assist those who are sick?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Compassion\n Love\n Faith\n Social justice and trust\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible\nVideo clip\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 76-77\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 45-46\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Guide learners to read Matthew 12:9-13\nStep 2: Guide learners in writing Matthew 12:13 on flash cards and recite it aloud in front of the class.\nStep 3: Emphasize to the learners the importance of kindness to the sickly and those with special needs\nStep 4: Educate learners on communicable diseases and how to avoid them, by observing personal hygiene and\nkeeping the environment clean\nSUMMARY\nReview the lesson and make summary.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to recite Matthew 12:13\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to visit the physically challenged in the company of their parents to pray with them and help them with\nhousehold chores..\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE EARLY LIFE OF JESUS CHRIST\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: EASTER.\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to discuss the death of Jesus as a sign of total love for human-kind\nand desire to love others.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy did Jesus die for us?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Compassion\n Love\n Faith\n Social justice and\ncourage\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 78-81\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 46-49\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Guide learners to read 1 Corinthians 15:3-4\nStep 2: Guide learners in mentioning what happens on Good Friday.\nStep 3: Guide learners to draw the cross.\nSUMMARY\nEaster is the day when Christ resurrected.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to read 1 Corinthians 15:3-4\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to accompany their parents to church on Good Friday and Easter festivals.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE EARLY LIFE OF JESUS CHRIST\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: EASTER.\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to discuss the death of Jesus as a sign of total love for human-kind\nand desire to love others.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy did Jesus die for us?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Compassion\n Love\n Faith\n Social justice and\ncourage\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 78-81\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 46-49\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Guide learners to read 1 Corinthians 15:3-4\nStep 2: Guide learners in mentioning what happens on Good Friday.\nStep 3: Guide learners to draw the cross.\nStep 4: Explain to the learners the importance of Jesus’ death and resurrection on Easter.\nSUMMARY\nReview the lesson and make summary\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to read 1 Corinthians 15:3-4\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to accompany their parents to church on Good Friday and Easter festivals.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS\nLESSON PLAN CRE ACTIVITES\nWeek:      Lesson:\nSCHOOL GRADE DATE TIME ROLL\nTWO\nSTRAND/THEME/TOPIC: THE EARLY LIFE OF JESUS CHRIST\nSUBSTRAND/SUB-THEME/SUB-TOPIC: EASTER.\nSpecific lesson learning outcome.\nBy the end of the lesson, the learner should be to discuss the death of Jesus as a sign of total love for human-kind\nand desire to love others and appreciate Jesus Christ’s death and resurrection as a way to salvation.\nKEY INQUIRY QUESTION (s)\nWhy did Jesus die for us?\nCore competencies Values PCIs\n Critical thinking\n Problem solving\n self-awareness\n Decision making\n Compassion\n Love\n Faith\n Social justice and\ncourage\nSelf-awareness\nSelf-esteem\nLEARNING RESOURCES\nBible\nC.R.E activities Learner’s Book Grade 2 pg. 78-81\nC.R.E Activities Teacher’s Guide Grade 2 pg. 46-49\nORGANIZATION OF LEARNING\nLearners to work in pairs or groups\nINTRODUCTION\nLearners to sing a familiar song\nLESSON DEVELOPMENT (Assessment as learning)\nStep 1: Guide learners to read 1 Corinthians 15:3-4\nStep 2: Guide learners in mentioning what happens on Good Friday.\nStep 3: Guide learners to mention what took place on Easter Monday, as they read Mark 16:5-6.\nStep 4: Explain to the learners the importance of Jesus’ death and resurrection on Easter.\nStep 5: Assist learners to understand how they are supposed to honour the death and resurrection of Jesus Christ\nduring Easter festivities\nSUMMARY\nJesus Christ loves us as human beings.\nCONCLUSION (Assessment of Learning)\nLearners to read 1 Corinthians 15:3-4\nEXTENSION OF ACTIVITIES\nLearners to accompany their parents to church on Good Friday and Easter festivals.\nREFLECTION ON THE LESSON/SELF-REMARKS", "ocrText": "", "imageOcrText": "", "imageCount": 0}
